Logging: SDD

Purpose:
  Defines logging policy and structured log format.

StructuredLog:
  Required: timestamp, level, service, environment, request_id,
            trace_id, operation, duration, error_code
  Optional: user_id, session_id, correlation_id, component, version

LogLevels:
  DEBUG: Development only, MUST NOT appear in production
  INFO: Normal operation events
  WARN: Recoverable issues
  ERROR: Failures affecting functionality
  FATAL: System-critical failures

SensitiveDataProtection:
  Forbidden: password, token, session, card, secret, PII,
             Authorization headers, Cookie values
  Action: Redact before logging, hash if needed for debugging
  Violation: SECURITY_VIOLATION

LogRetention:
  Development: 7 days
  Production: 30 days
  Compliance: As required by regulation

Rules:
  [LG1] All errors MUST be logged with context.
  [LG2] All security events MUST be logged.
  [LG3] Logs MUST include tenant_id, correlation_id, actor_id.
  [LG4] Sensitive data MUST NOT appear in logs.

State: +